GIVEN `the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      consequence IS A `forms 6 to 11.1 consequence of the offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 9 if the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3), the Form states that` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person commits an offence under subsection 145(3)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you commit an offence under subsection 145(3) of the Criminal Code"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER consequence
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 a warrant for the arrest of the person may be issued` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to a fine` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to imprisonment` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to both a fine and imprisonment` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 another consequence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence names a warrant for arrest and "you may be liable to a fine or to imprisonment, or to both", and does not say "only"

-- It is not a lawful excuse to an offence under subsection 145(3) of the Criminal Code that this appearance notice does not accurately describe the offence that you are alleged to have committed (subsection 145(6) of the Criminal Code).
-- A flat negative ("It is not a lawful excuse"): the one ground it names is JUST FALSE as an excuse; any other ground is not addressed (NOTHING).
-- src:18098 | It is not a lawful excuse to an offence under subsection 145(3) of the Criminal Code that this appearance notice does not accurately describe the offence that you are alleged to have committed (subsection 145(6) of the Criminal Code).
@ref Form 9 (Section 2) Appearance Notice, an inaccurate description is not a lawful excuse (src:18098)
GIVEN `the excuse offered is that the appearance notice does not accurately describe the offence that the person is alleged to have committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 9 the inaccuracy of the description is a lawful excuse to an offence under subsection 145(3)` MEANS
    IF `the excuse offered is that the appearance notice does not accurately describe the offence that the person is alleged to have committed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is not a lawful excuse to an offence under subsection 145(3) of the Criminal Code that this appearance notice does not accurately describe the offence that you are alleged to have committed"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that this appearance notice does not accurately describe the offence that you are alleged to have committed"

-- If you do not comply with this appearance notice or are charged with committing an offence after you have been released, this appearance notice may be cancelled and, as a result, you may be detained in custody (subsections 524(4) and (6.2) of the Criminal Code).
-- "If you do not comply ... or are charged ...": either limb suffices. "may be cancelled" is a power limited by its "If": neither limb met is NOTHING (fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
-- "as a result, you may be detained" is a result of the cancellation only.
-- src:18099 | If you do not comply with this appearance notice or are charged with committing an offence after you have been released, this appearance notice may be cancelled and, as a result, you may be detained in custody (subsections 524(4) and (6.2) of the Criminal Code).
@ref Form 9 (Section 2) Appearance Notice, cancellation and detention (src:18099)
GIVEN `the person does not comply with the appearance notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is charged with committing an offence after the person has been released` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 9 the appearance notice may be cancelled` MEANS
    IF `the person does not comply with the appearance notice` OR `the person is charged with committing an offence after the person has been released`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If you do not comply with this appearance notice or are charged with committing an offence after you have been released"

-- src:18099 | If you do not comply with this appearance notice or are charged with committing an offence after you have been released, this appearance notice may be cancelled and, as a result, you may be detained in custody (subsections 524(4) and (6.2) of the Criminal Code).
@ref Form 9 (Section 2) Appearance Notice, cancellation and detention (src:18099)
GIVEN `the appearance notice has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 9 the person may be detained in custody as a result of the cancellation` MEANS
    IF `the appearance notice has been cancelled`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as a result, you may be detained in custody"

§ `Form 10 -- Undertaking`

-- 4 Mandatory Condition: You must attend court as indicated below, and afterwards as required by the court:
-- The mandatory condition. The days until the date, time and court indicated are the input.
-- src:18121 | You must attend court as indicated below, and afterwards as required by the court:
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, the duty to attend or appear (src:18121)
GIVEN `the days until the day set out in the document` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `forms 6 to 11.1 action`
`form 10 the accused must attend court` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `form 10 attends court as required`
    WITHIN `the days until the day set out in the document`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the accused`
         BECAUSE "Form 10: the person did not attend or appear as the Form requires (the Form warns of the offence, the warrant for arrest and the cancellation it describes)"

DECLARE `form 10 purpose of a condition` IS ONE OF
    `form 10 to ensure the accused's attendance in court`
    `form 10 to ensure the safety and security of a victim of the offence`
    `form 10 to ensure the safety and security of a witness to the offence`
    `form 10 to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence`
    `form 10 to prevent the commission of another offence`
    `form 10 none of those purposes`

-- "You must also comply with any conditions that are indicated below by a check mark (check only those that are reasonable in the circumstances of the offence and necessary, to ensure the accused’s attendance
-- in court or the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence, or to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence or the commission of another offence):"
-- First limb: the person must comply with a condition that is checked; an unchecked condition is outside the sentence's words (NOTHING).
-- src:18127 | You must also comply with any conditions that are indicated below by a check mark (check only those that are reasonable in the circumstances of the offence and necessary, to ensure the accused’s attendance in court or the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence, or to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence or the commission of another offence):
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, item 5 Additional Conditions, the conditions checked (src:18127)
GIVEN `the condition is indicated by a check mark` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10 item 5 the person must comply with the condition` MEANS
    IF `the condition is indicated by a check mark`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any conditions that are indicated below by a check mark"

-- Second limb, "check only those that are reasonable ... and necessary, to ensure ...": "only" closes it, so a condition that is not reasonable, or not necessary for one of the five purposes, may not be checked (JUST FALSE).
-- src:18127 | You must also comply with any conditions that are indicated below by a check mark (check only those that are reasonable in the circumstances of the offence and necessary, to ensure the accused’s attendance in court or the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence, or to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence or the commission of another offence):
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, item 5 Additional Conditions, which conditions may be checked (src:18127)
GIVEN `the condition is reasonable in the circumstances of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `form 10 purpose of a condition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10 item 5 a condition may be checked` MEANS
    IF NOT `the condition is reasonable in the circumstances of the offence`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "check only those that are reasonable in the circumstances of the offence and necessary"
    ELSE
        CONSIDER purpose
        WHEN `form 10 to ensure the accused's attendance in court` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `form 10 to ensure the safety and security of a victim of the offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `form 10 to ensure the safety and security of a witness to the offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `form 10 to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `form 10 to prevent the commission of another offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `form 10 none of those purposes` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "check only those that are reasonable in the circumstances of the offence and necessary, to ensure the accused’s attendance in court or the safety and security of any victim of or witness to the offence, or to prevent the continuation or repetition of the offence or the commission of another offence"

-- The weapons condition, checked: the things the person "must not possess" and "must surrender" (Form 10 paragraph (i); Form 11 says "crossbow" for "cross-bow" and "any of them" for "those").
DECLARE `forms 10 and 11 thing in the weapons condition` IS ONE OF
    `forms 10 and 11 a firearm`
    `forms 10 and 11 a cross-bow`
    `forms 10 and 11 a prohibited weapon`
    `forms 10 and 11 a restricted weapon`
    `forms 10 and 11 a prohibited device`
    `forms 10 and 11 a firearm part`
    `forms 10 and 11 ammunition`
    `forms 10 and 11 prohibited ammunition`
    `forms 10 and 11 an explosive substance`
    `forms 10 and 11 an authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling the acquisition or possession of a firearm`
    `forms 10 and 11 something else`

-- "(i) You must not possess a firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance ..."
-- The nine things are named; the document is not something one "must not possess" (it is to be surrendered); a thing the list does not name is not covered (list not closed).
-- src:18136 | □ (i) You must not possess a firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance and you must surrender those that are in your possession and also any authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling you to acquire or possess them to (name or title) at (place).
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, item 5 paragraph (i), what the person must not possess (src:18136)
GIVEN thing IS A `forms 10 and 11 thing in the weapons condition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must not possess the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 a firearm` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 a cross-bow` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 a prohibited weapon` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 a restricted weapon` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 a prohibited device` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 a firearm part` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 ammunition` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 prohibited ammunition` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 an explosive substance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 an authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling the acquisition or possession of a firearm` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "You must not possess a firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance"
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence names nine things and does not say "only"

-- "... and you must surrender those that are in your possession and also any authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling you to acquire or possess them to (name or title) at (place)."
-- src:18136 | □ (i) You must not possess a firearm, cross-bow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance and you must surrender those that are in your possession and also any authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling you to acquire or possess them to (name or title) at (place).
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, item 5 paragraph (i), what the person must surrender (src:18136)
GIVEN thing IS A `forms 10 and 11 thing in the weapons condition`
      `the thing is in the person's possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10 item 5 paragraph (i) the person must surrender the thing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the thing is in the person's possession`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "those that are in your possession"
        IF thing EQUALS `forms 10 and 11 something else`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence names the things and the documents and does not say "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "(j) You promise to pay the amount of (not more than $500), if you fail to comply with a condition of this undertaking."
-- src:18137 | □ (j) You promise to pay the amount of (not more than $500), if you fail to comply with a condition of this undertaking.
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, item 5 paragraph (j), the amount promised (src:18137)
GIVEN `the amount the person is to promise to pay, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10 item 5 paragraph (j) the amount the person may be required to promise to pay is within the limit` MEANS
    IF `the amount the person is to promise to pay, in dollars` AT MOST 500
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(not more than $500)"

-- "(k) You must deposit money or other valuable security whose value is equal to the amount of (not more than $500) with (name or title), because you are not ordinarily resident in the province or do not reside
-- within 200 km of the place in which you are in custody." The amount is capped at $500; the stated ground ("because") limits the grant, so a person who is resident and within 200 km is outside it (NOTHING).
-- src:18138 | □ (k) You must deposit money or other valuable security whose value is equal to the amount of (not more than $500) with (name or title), because you are not ordinarily resident in the province or do not reside within 200 km of the place in which you are in custody.
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, item 5 paragraph (k), the deposit (src:18138)
GIVEN `the amount of money or valuable security to be deposited, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is ordinarily resident in the province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the distance in kilometres between the place in which the person is in custody and the place where the person resides` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10 item 5 paragraph (k) the person may be required to make the deposit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of money or valuable security to be deposited, in dollars` GREATER THAN 500
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(not more than $500)"
        IF `the person is ordinarily resident in the province`
           AND `the distance in kilometres between the place in which the person is in custody and the place where the person resides` AT MOST 200
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "because you are not ordinarily resident in the province or do not reside within 200 km of the place in which you are in custody"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "The conditions of this undertaking may be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor and yourself."  Both consents give the route; a missing consent is outside it (NOTHING), because the next sentences give other routes.
-- src:18143 | The conditions of this undertaking may be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor and yourself. In addition, you or the prosecutor may apply to a justice of the peace to replace this undertaking with a release order under section 515 of the Criminal Code. Finally, you or the prosecutor may apply to a justice of the peace to vary this undertaking.
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, item 7 Variation and Replacement (src:18143)
GIVEN `the prosecutor consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10 item 7 the conditions may be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor and the person` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor consents in writing` AND `the person consents in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the written consent of the prosecutor and yourself"

-- "In addition, you or the prosecutor may apply to a justice of the peace to replace this undertaking with a release order under section 515 of the Criminal Code."
-- src:18143 | The conditions of this undertaking may be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor and yourself. In addition, you or the prosecutor may apply to a justice of the peace to replace this undertaking with a release order under section 515 of the Criminal Code. Finally, you or the prosecutor may apply to a justice of the peace to vary this undertaking.
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, item 7 Variation and Replacement (src:18143)
GIVEN `the applicant is the person or the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10 item 7 the applicant may apply to a justice of the peace to replace the undertaking with a release order under section 515` MEANS
    IF `the applicant is the person or the prosecutor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "you or the prosecutor may apply to a justice of the peace to replace this undertaking"

-- "Finally, you or the prosecutor may apply to a justice of the peace to vary this undertaking."
-- src:18143 | The conditions of this undertaking may be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor and yourself. In addition, you or the prosecutor may apply to a justice of the peace to replace this undertaking with a release order under section 515 of the Criminal Code. Finally, you or the prosecutor may apply to a justice of the peace to vary this undertaking.
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, item 7 Variation and Replacement (src:18143)
GIVEN `the applicant is the person or the prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10 item 7 the applicant may apply to a justice of the peace to vary the undertaking` MEANS
    IF `the applicant is the person or the prosecutor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "you or the prosecutor may apply to a justice of the peace to vary this undertaking"

-- "... remain in effect until ...": an "until" bar (JUST TRUE before the end, JUST FALSE once an ending event has happened).
-- src:18145 | The mandatory condition and the conditions indicated by a check mark on this undertaking remain in effect until they are cancelled or changed or until you have been discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court (sections 763 and 764 of the Criminal Code).
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, how long the conditions remain in effect (src:18145)
GIVEN `the conditions have been cancelled or changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10 the conditions remain in effect` MEANS
    IF `the conditions have been cancelled or changed` OR `the person has been discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until they are cancelled or changed or until you have been discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- You are warned that, unless you have a lawful excuse, you commit an offence under section 145 of the Criminal Code if you fail to follow any of the conditions set out in this undertaking, including (a) to fail to attend court as required; (b) to fail to appear as required for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act; (c) to fail to remain in the territorial jurisdiction ... (if applicable).
-- "if you fail to follow any of the conditions": an "if" (JUST FALSE when unmet); "unless you have a lawful excuse" (JUST FALSE, once met: NOTES.md F-B).
-- src:18147 | You are warned that, unless you have a lawful excuse, you commit an offence under section 145 of the Criminal Code if you fail to follow any of the conditions set out in this undertaking, including
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, the warning of the offence (src:18147)
GIVEN `the person failed to follow any of the conditions set out in the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10 warning: unless the person has a lawful excuse, failing to follow any of the conditions is an offence under section 145` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless you have a lawful excuse"
        IF NOT `the person failed to follow any of the conditions set out in the undertaking`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if you fail to follow any of the conditions set out in this undertaking"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- If you commit an offence under section 145 of the Criminal Code, a warrant for your arrest may be issued (section 512 or 512.2 of the Criminal Code) and you may be liable to a fine or to imprisonment, or to both.
-- "If" unmet: JUST FALSE. A consequence the sentence does not list: not covered (the list is not closed with "only").
-- src:18151 | If you commit an offence under section 145 of the Criminal Code, a warrant for your arrest may be issued (section 512 or 512.2 of the Criminal Code) and you may be liable to a fine or to imprisonment, or to both.
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, what may follow an offence (src:18151)
GIVEN `the person commits an offence under section 145` IS A BOOLEAN
      consequence IS A `forms 6 to 11.1 consequence of the offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10 if the person commits an offence under section 145, the Form states that` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person commits an offence under section 145`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you commit an offence under section 145 of the Criminal Code"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER consequence
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 a warrant for the arrest of the person may be issued` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to a fine` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to imprisonment` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to both a fine and imprisonment` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 another consequence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence names a warrant for arrest and "you may be liable to a fine or to imprisonment, or to both", and does not say "only"

-- It is not a lawful excuse to an offence under subsection 145(4) of the Criminal Code that this undertaking does not accurately describe the offence that you are alleged to have committed (subsection 145(6) of the Criminal Code).
-- A flat negative ("It is not a lawful excuse"): the one ground it names is JUST FALSE as an excuse; any other ground is not addressed (NOTHING).
-- src:18152 | It is not a lawful excuse to an offence under subsection 145(4) of the Criminal Code that this undertaking does not accurately describe the offence that you are alleged to have committed (subsection 145(6) of the Criminal Code).
@ref Form 10 (Section 2) Undertaking, an inaccurate description is not a lawful excuse (src:18152)
GIVEN `the excuse offered is that the undertaking does not accurately describe the offence that the person is alleged to have committed` IS A BOOLEAN
