`form 10 the inaccuracy of the description is a lawful excuse to an offence under subsection 145(4)` MEANS
    IF `the excuse offered is that the undertaking does not accurately describe the offence that the person is alleged to have committed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is not a lawful excuse to an offence under subsection 145(4) of the Criminal Code that this undertaking does not accurately describe the offence that you are alleged to have committed"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "that this undertaking does not accurately describe the offence that you are alleged to have committed"

-- If you do not comply with this undertaking or are charged with committing an offence after you have been released, this undertaking may be cancelled and, as a result, you may be detained in custody (subsections 524(4) and (6.2) of the Criminal Code).
-- "If you do not comply ... or are charged ...": either limb suffices. "may be cancelled" is a power limited by its "If": neither limb met is NOTHING (fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
-- "as a result, you may be detained" is a result of the cancellation only.
-- src:18153 | If you do not comply with this undertaking or are charged with committing an offence after you have been released, this undertaking may be cancelled and, as a result, you may be detained in custody (subsections 524(4) and (6.2) of the Criminal Code).
