GIVEN `the person does not comply with the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is charged with committing an offence after the person has been released` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10 the undertaking may be cancelled` MEANS
    IF `the person does not comply with the undertaking` OR `the person is charged with committing an offence after the person has been released`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If you do not comply with this undertaking or are charged with committing an offence after you have been released"

-- src:18153 | If you do not comply with this undertaking or are charged with committing an offence after you have been released, this undertaking may be cancelled and, as a result, you may be detained in custody (subsections 524(4) and (6.2) of the Criminal Code).
