§ `Form 10.1 -- Undertaking (witness)`

-- 4 Mandatory Condition: You must attend court as indicated below, and afterwards as required by the court:
-- The actor is the core's `a witness`. The days until the date, time and court indicated are the input.
-- src:18177 | You must attend court as indicated below, and afterwards as required by the court:
@ref Form 10.1 (Subsection 705(4)) Undertaking — Witness, the duty to attend or appear (src:18177)
GIVEN `the days until the day set out in the document` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `forms 6 to 11.1 action`
`form 10.1 the witness must attend court` MEANS
    PARTY `a witness`
    MUST `form 10.1 attends court as required`
    WITHIN `the days until the day set out in the document`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a witness`
         BECAUSE "Form 10.1: the person did not attend or appear as the Form requires (the Form warns of the offence, the warrant for arrest and the cancellation it describes)"

-- "The mandatory condition and the conditions determined by the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge on this undertaking remain in effect until they are cancelled or changed or until you appear and
-- remain in attendance at the proceeding as required by the mandatory condition (section 763 of the Criminal Code)."
