    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until they are cancelled or changed or until you appear and remain in attendance at the proceeding as required by the mandatory condition"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- "The conditions of this undertaking may be varied by application to the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge."
-- src:18187 | The conditions of this undertaking may be varied by application to the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge.
@ref Form 10.1 (Subsection 705(4)) Undertaking -- Witness, item 7 variation (src:18187)
GIVEN `an application is made to the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10.1 the conditions may be varied by application` MEANS
    IF `an application is made to the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be varied by application to the court, judge, justice or provincial court judge"

-- You are warned that, unless you have a lawful excuse, you commit an offence under section 145 of the Criminal Code if you fail to follow any of the conditions set out in this undertaking, including (a) if you fail to attend court as required; or (b) if you fail to comply with the conditions determined by the court ...
-- "if you fail to follow any of the conditions": an "if" (JUST FALSE when unmet); "unless you have a lawful excuse" (JUST FALSE, once met: NOTES.md F-B).
-- src:18189 | You are warned that, unless you have a lawful excuse, you commit an offence under section 145 of the Criminal Code if you fail to follow any of the conditions set out in this undertaking, including
@ref Form 10.1 (Subsection 705(4)) Undertaking — Witness, the warning of the offence (src:18189)
GIVEN `the person failed to follow any of the conditions set out in the undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10.1 warning: unless the person has a lawful excuse, failing to follow any of the conditions is an offence under section 145` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless you have a lawful excuse"
        IF NOT `the person failed to follow any of the conditions set out in the undertaking`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if you fail to follow any of the conditions set out in this undertaking"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- If you commit an offence under section 145 of the Criminal Code, a warrant for your arrest may be issued (section 512 or 512.2 of the Criminal Code) and you may be liable to a fine or to imprisonment, or to both.
-- "If" unmet: JUST FALSE. A consequence the sentence does not list: not covered (the list is not closed with "only").
-- src:18192 | If you commit an offence under section 145 of the Criminal Code, a warrant for your arrest may be issued (section 512 or 512.2 of the Criminal Code) and you may be liable to a fine or to imprisonment, or to both.
@ref Form 10.1 (Subsection 705(4)) Undertaking — Witness, what may follow an offence (src:18192)
GIVEN `the person commits an offence under section 145` IS A BOOLEAN
      consequence IS A `forms 6 to 11.1 consequence of the offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 10.1 if the person commits an offence under section 145, the Form states that` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person commits an offence under section 145`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you commit an offence under section 145 of the Criminal Code"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER consequence
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 a warrant for the arrest of the person may be issued` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to a fine` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to imprisonment` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to both a fine and imprisonment` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 another consequence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence names a warrant for arrest and "you may be liable to a fine or to imprisonment, or to both", and does not say "only"

-- "I understand that I do not have to accept the conditions and that, if I do not accept the conditions, I will be brought before a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice under sections 705 and 706 of the Criminal Code."
-- The first limb is a flat statement of a liberty (JUST TRUE); the second is conditional on not accepting ("if" unmet: JUST FALSE).
-- src:18196 | I understand that I do not have to accept the conditions and that, if I do not accept the conditions, I will be brought before a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice under sections 705 and 706 of the Criminal Code.
@ref Form 10.1 (Subsection 705(4)) Undertaking — Witness, the person need not accept the conditions (src:18196)
