§ `Form 11 -- Release order`

-- "In order for you to be released, the obligations that are indicated below by a check mark must be complied with."
-- A necessary condition: not complied with, the person is not released (JUST FALSE); complied with, the sentence does not say the person is released (NOTHING): it states what is needed, not what is enough.
-- src:18217 | In order for you to be released, the obligations that are indicated below by a check mark must be complied with.
@ref Form 11 (Section 2) Release Order, item 4 Financial Obligations (src:18217)
GIVEN `every obligation indicated by a check mark has been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 11 item 4 the person is released` MEANS
    IF `every obligation indicated by a check mark has been complied with`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In order for you to be released, the obligations that are indicated below by a check mark must be complied with" states what is necessary, not what is enough
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In order for you to be released, the obligations that are indicated below by a check mark must be complied with"

-- "You must comply with the conditions that are indicated below by a check mark."
-- src:18222 | You must comply with the conditions that are indicated below by a check mark.
@ref Form 11 (Section 2) Release Order, item 5 Conditions (src:18222)
GIVEN `the condition is indicated by a check mark` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 11 item 5 the person must comply with the condition` MEANS
    IF `the condition is indicated by a check mark`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the conditions that are indicated below by a check mark"

-- "You must not possess a firearm, crossbow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance and you must surrender any of them in your
-- possession and any authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling the acquisition or possession of a firearm to (name or title) at (place)."
-- src:18229 | □ You must not possess a firearm, crossbow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance and you must surrender any of them in your possession and any authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling the acquisition or possession of a firearm to (name or title) at (place).
@ref Form 11 (Section 2) Release Order, item 5 the weapons condition, what the person must not possess (src:18229)
GIVEN thing IS A `forms 10 and 11 thing in the weapons condition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 11 item 5 the weapons condition: the person must not possess the thing` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 a firearm` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 a cross-bow` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 a prohibited weapon` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 a restricted weapon` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 a prohibited device` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 a firearm part` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 ammunition` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 prohibited ammunition` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 an explosive substance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 an authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling the acquisition or possession of a firearm` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "You must not possess a firearm, crossbow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance"
    WHEN `forms 10 and 11 something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence names nine things and does not say "only"

-- src:18229 | □ You must not possess a firearm, crossbow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance and you must surrender any of them in your possession and any authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling the acquisition or possession of a firearm to (name or title) at (place).
@ref Form 11 (Section 2) Release Order, item 5 the weapons condition, what the person must surrender (src:18229)
GIVEN thing IS A `forms 10 and 11 thing in the weapons condition`
      `the thing is in the person's possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 11 item 5 the weapons condition: the person must surrender the thing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the thing is in the person's possession`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "you must surrender any of them in your possession"
        IF thing EQUALS `forms 10 and 11 something else`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence names the things and the documents and does not say "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "The conditions of this release order may be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor, yourself and your sureties, if any."
-- src:18233 | The conditions of this release order may be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor, yourself and your sureties, if any. In addition, you or the prosecutor may apply to a judge to have any condition in this release order cancelled or changed.
@ref Form 11 (Section 2) Release Order, item 6 Variation (src:18233)
GIVEN `the prosecutor consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has sureties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sureties consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 11 item 6 the conditions may be varied with the written consent of the prosecutor, the person and the sureties, if any` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor consents in writing` AND `the person consents in writing` AND ((NOT `the person has sureties`) OR `the sureties consent in writing`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the written consent of the prosecutor, yourself and your sureties, if any"

-- "In addition, you or the prosecutor may apply to a judge to have any condition in this release order cancelled or changed."
