            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to imprisonment` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 the person may be liable to both a fine and imprisonment` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 6 to 11.1 another consequence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sentence names a warrant for arrest and "you may be liable to a fine or to imprisonment, or to both", and does not say "only"

-- If you do not comply with this release order or are charged with committing an offence after you have been released, this release order may be cancelled and, as a result, you may be detained in custody (subsections 524(4) and (6.2) of the Criminal Code).
-- "If you do not comply ... or are charged ...": either limb suffices. "may be cancelled" is a power limited by its "If": neither limb met is NOTHING (fork F-W; the other reading, a failed "If" as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE).
-- "as a result, you may be detained" is a result of the cancellation only.
-- src:18239 | If you do not comply with this release order or are charged with committing an offence after you have been released, this release order may be cancelled and, as a result, you may be detained in custody (subsections 524(4) and (6.2) of the Criminal Code).
