§ `Form 11.1 -- Order to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act`

-- You are ordered, in Her Majesty’s name, to appear on (date) at (hour) at (place) for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act.
-- The actor is the core's `the accused`: the person is subject to a release order. The days until the day set out are the input.
-- src:18270 | You are ordered, in Her Majesty’s name, to appear on (date) at (hour) at (place) for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act.
@ref Form 11.1 (Section 515.01) Order to Appear for the Purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act, the duty to attend or appear (src:18270)
GIVEN `the days until the day set out in the document` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `forms 6 to 11.1 action`
`form 11.1 the accused must appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` MEANS
    PARTY `the accused`
    MUST `form 11.1 appears for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act`
    WITHIN `the days until the day set out in the document`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the accused`
         BECAUSE "Form 11.1: the person did not attend or appear as the Form requires (the Form warns of the offence, the warrant for arrest and the cancellation it describes)"

-- You are warned that, unless you have a lawful excuse, it is an offence under subsection 145(2) of the Criminal Code to fail to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act, as required by this order.
-- A person who did not fail to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act, as required by the order is outside the sentence's words (NOTHING); a lawful excuse is "unless you have a lawful excuse" (JUST FALSE, once met: NOTES.md F-B).
-- src:18272 | You are warned that, unless you have a lawful excuse, it is an offence under subsection 145(2) of the Criminal Code to fail to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act, as required by this order.
@ref Form 11.1 (Section 515.01) Order to Appear for the Purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act, the warning of the offence (src:18272)
