§ `Form 12 -- Surety declaration`

-- "I understand that the accused has also been charged with (set out briefly the offence ...), but this declaration does not apply to those charges."
-- A flat negative: the declaration does not apply to the other charges (JUST FALSE as to its application). Where the second box is not the one ticked, the sentence is not addressed (NOTHING).
-- src:18308 | □ I understand that the accused has also been charged with (set out briefly the offence in respect of which the accused was charged), but this declaration does not apply to those charges.
@ref Form 12 (Section 515.1) Surety Declaration, item 5 Other Outstanding Charges against the Accused (src:18308)
GIVEN `the accused has also been charged with another offence, as the second box of item 5 says` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 12 item 5 the declaration applies to the other outstanding charges` MEANS
    IF `the accused has also been charged with another offence, as the second box of item 5 says`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this declaration does not apply to those charges"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the first box says the accused has no other outstanding charge, so there are none to which the declaration could apply or not apply

-- "I understand that failure on the part of the accused to follow any of the conditions in their release order or recognizance could lead to the forfeiture of the amount of money that has been promised or deposited."
-- src:18319 | I understand that failure on the part of the accused to follow any of the conditions in their release order or recognizance could lead to the forfeiture of the amount of money that has been promised or deposited.
@ref Form 12 (Section 515.1) Surety Declaration, item 8 Acknowledgment (src:18319)
