    IF `the accused failed to follow any of the conditions in their release order or recognizance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "failure on the part of the accused to follow any of the conditions in their release order or recognizance could lead to the forfeiture"

DECLARE `form 12 way of ceasing to be a surety` IS ONE OF
    `form 12 by making an application`
    `form 12 by bringing the accused to the court in order to be discharged from the surety's obligation (section 767)`
    `form 12 by taking and giving the accused into custody (section 768)`
    `form 12 in another way`

-- "I understand that I may, at any time, ask to no longer be a surety by making an application, by bringing the accused to the court in order to be discharged from my obligation (section 767 of the Criminal Code) or
-- by taking and giving the accused into custody (section 768 of the Criminal Code)."  "at any time": no period limits it. Three ways are named; another way is not covered (the list is not closed with "only").
-- src:18320 | I understand that I may, at any time, ask to no longer be a surety by making an application, by bringing the accused to the court in order to be discharged from my obligation (section 767 of the Criminal Code) or by taking and giving the accused into custody (section 768 of the Criminal Code).
@ref Form 12 (Section 515.1) Surety Declaration, item 8 Acknowledgment (src:18320)
GIVEN way IS A `form 12 way of ceasing to be a surety`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 12 item 8 the surety may, at any time, ask to no longer be a surety` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `form 12 by making an application` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 12 by bringing the accused to the court in order to be discharged from the surety's obligation (section 767)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 12 by taking and giving the accused into custody (section 768)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `form 12 in another way` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): three ways are named and the sentence does not say "only"

